    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1155">

                <pb facs="1066" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/2910</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 2, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.50 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>According to reliable information six submarine destroyers for British loaded
                    aboard steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Bohemian</hi>, sailing from Boston early
                    to-day. On account of violation Article 8, thirteenth Hague convention, would be
                    obliged for kind immediate investigation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
